# Promising Stairs counts "different names among unlocked doors of Rooms you control" (CR 201.2b, 709.5): two Rooms with the same
# unlocked doors give their names once. Bot1 unlocks eight doors, but two Bottomless Pool // Locker Room cards share theirs: Promising
# Stairs and Unholy Annex on turn 1 (Black Lotus, three Moxen), both Bottomless Pools on turn 3, the first Locker Room on turn 5,
# Ritual Chamber on turn 7, the second Locker Room on turn 9 and Central Elevator on turn 11. At turn 13's upkeep eight doors are
# unlocked with six different names among them, and Bot1 does not win (counting each door would). The surveil keeps the top card.

